# opponent-discards-on-turn at turn 2: "At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if it's that player's second turn, that
# player discards a card." Bot2's second turn is turn 4: it chooses and discards its Mountain (CR 701.9a). Bot2's first
# upkeep (turn 2) and third (turn 6) have no trigger, nor has Bot1's own second upkeep (turn 3): the turn must be an
# opponent's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest x40

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mountain
Island x38

[Variant]
Bot1: maximum 20; emblem Gear test: opponent-discards-on-turn, turn 2
Bot2: maximum 20

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Stack = Gear test: opponent-discards-on-turn, turn 2
Bot2.Choose(Mountain)
[T6 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Mountain
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
